Redproof-Patch: own-canary-key-unmapped
Redproof-Family: ownership
Redproof-Run: TestEveryLiveCanaryKeyIsMappedInTheWorkflow
Redproof-Package: ./internal/canary
Redproof-Expect: EVEN AFTER the operator sets the repository secret
Redproof-Summary: A canary key the live-canary workflow does not map — SENTRY_DSN removed from the job env. The suite stays green: the row simply skips as [inapplicable] in every run forever, reporting a clean line while checking nothing. The expensive part is that the operator cannot fix it — they set CANARY_SENTRY_DSN, the row keeps skipping because nothing carries the secret into the job, and the skip reason names the key as missing, so a true sentence about a credential they already supplied reads as a broken canary. The refusal must state that consequence, not the mismatch.
diff --git a/.github/workflows/live-canary.yml b/.github/workflows/live-canary.yml
--- a/.github/workflows/live-canary.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/live-canary.yml
@@ -104,7 +104,6 @@
 
       # ggg/observability — ggg/system/observability-sentry@sentry. Leaves one
       # immutable event per run; point it at a throwaway project.
-      SENTRY_DSN: ${{ secrets.CANARY_SENTRY_DSN }}
 
       # ggg/llm — ggg/system/llm-openai-compatible@openai. Spends tokens.
       LLM_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.CANARY_LLM_API_KEY }}
